# flywheel-agent-b-rework-loop

Executes Agent B's mandatory rework loop when the Validation Engineer Agent (C) rejects an assembled flywheel unit.

## Procedures
- 1. Receive failed unit back from Validation Engineer (C) via Forklift Operator (D).
- 2. Review rejection notes from Validation Engineer (C).
- 3. Disassemble affected components (avoid full teardown if possible).
- 4. Correct identified issues: check bearing seating, tighten fasteners, verify alignment.
- 5. Reassemble with more attention to detail.
- 6. Perform extra-careful basic spin test.
- 7. Return unit to Validation Engineer (C) for re-testing.
- 8. Repeat loop until unit passes validation.

## Conventions
- Agent B cannot refuse rework requests from Agent C — compliance is mandatory.
- Avoid full teardown unless necessary; targeted disassembly of affected components is preferred.
- Each rework cycle still requires an extra-careful basic spin test before returning to Agent C.

## Assets
- flywheel-protocols.md

